package "pkg/fvcb"

// This dep is LLVM-compiled under `-backend native` (only the main module honors
// --backend native; dependency packages always go through the LLVM backend).  It
// is the package that CREATES the func value — GetSliceCallback takes the ADDRESS of
// the package-private sumSlice (an OP_FUNC_VALUE), so the per-function
// `@__shim.<mangled>` LLVM func-value shim is emitted HERE, in the DEP.  main never
// takes that address, so main emits NO shim for it (see the test's main.bn):
// main only DISPATCHES the returned
// func value through its vtable.call slot, which points at THIS dep's LLVM-emitted
// shim.  That makes 1006 the TRUE native-dispatch -> LLVM-EMITTED-shim litmus,
// distinct from 1003 (where main takes the address itself and thus builds its OWN
// native shim, so the dispatch reaches a native shim, not the LLVM one).

// GetSliceCallback returns a *func value over the package-private sumSlice, which
// takes a raw slice (*[]int, an 8-byte NON-coerced 2-word in-register aggregate)
// BY VALUE.  The LLVM shim for sumSlice declares the slice arg i8* (by-address:
// SizeOf 8 > PointerSize 4 on ILP32, <= AggregateInRegMax), so native main's
// dispatch MUST pass the slice BY-ADDRESS (isByAddressAggArm32 true — the PIECE 2
// genuinely-non-coerced case) for the two words to arrive intact.
func GetSliceCallback() *func(*[]int) int
